  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Isaiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 52,
    "summary": "In the last days, Zion will return, and Israel will be redeemed—The Messiah will deal prudently and be exalted.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Awake, awake; put on thy strength, O Zion; put on thy beautiful garments, O Jerusalem, the holy city: for henceforth there shall no more come into thee the uncircumcised and the unclean.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "3 Ne. 20:36 (36–38)."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Israel, Restoration of; Mission of Latter-day Saints; Priesthood, Power of; Strength."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Zion."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "D&C 113:7–8."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "D&C 82:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Jerusalem."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Shake thyself from the dust; arise, and sit down, O Jerusalem: loose thyself from the bands of thy neck, O captive daughter of Zion.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "Isa. 51:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "IE Arise from the dust and sit down in dignity, being redeemed at last."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "D&C 113:10. TG Bondage, Spiritual."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For thus saith the Lord, Ye have sold yourselves for nought; and ye shall be redeemed without money.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Israel."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "Isa. 45:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For thus saith the Lord God, My people went down aforetime into Egypt to sojourn there; and the Assyrian oppressed them without cause.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "HEB Jehovah."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Gen. 46:6 (2–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now therefore, what have I here, saith the Lord, that my people is taken away for nought? they that rule over them make them to howl, saith the Lord; and my name continually every day is blasphemed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 197,
            "text": "TG Blaspheme."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 184,
            "end": 186
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore my people shall know my name: therefore they shall know in that day that I am he that doth speak: behold, it is I.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Isa. 2:11; Hosea 2:16 (14–23); Zech. 9:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 65
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 87
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 121
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace; that bringeth good tidings of good, that publisheth salvation; that saith unto Zion, Thy God reigneth!",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Beauty."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Dispensations."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Gospel."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "Isa. 40:9; Mosiah 15:14 (13–18); D&C 128:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "TG Missionary Work."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "TG Peace; Peacemakers."
          },
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 187,
            "text": "TG Zion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy watchmen shall lift up the voice; with the voice together shall they sing: for they shall see eye to eye, when the Lord shall bring again Zion.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Watchman."
          },
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "D&C 84:98."
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 141,
            "text": "HEB returns to Zion, or restores Zion. TG Millennium, Preparing a People for."
          },
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 146,
            "text": "D&C 12:6; 39:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Break forth into joy, sing together, ye waste places of Jerusalem: for the Lord hath comforted his people, he hath redeemed Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "OR ruins."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord hath made bare his holy arm in the eyes of all the nations; and all the ends of the earth shall see the salvation of our God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "1 Ne. 22:10 (10–11); D&C 133:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG God, Power of."
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Second Coming."
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "TG Salvation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Depart ye, depart ye, go ye out from thence, touch no unclean thing; go ye out of the midst of her; be ye clean, that bear the vessels of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "D&C 38:42."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "2 Tim. 2:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Isa. 48:20; 2 Cor. 6:17 (14–17); Rev. 18:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "TG Separation."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Priesthood, Qualifying for; Purity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye shall not go out with haste, nor go by flight: for the Lord will go before you; and the God of Israel will be your rearward.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Haste."
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "OR rearguard. D&C 49:27."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 116
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, my servant shall deal prudently, he shall be exalted and extolled, and be very high.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As many were astonied at thee; his visage was so marred more than any man, and his form more than the sons of men:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "OR astonished."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "OR appearance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "So shall he sprinkle many nations; the kings shall shut their mouths at him: for that which had not been told them shall they see; and that which they had not heard shall they consider.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "JST Isa. 52:15 … gather … Ezek. 36:25; 1 Pet. 1:2."
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "Rom. 15:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 85
          },
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 139
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
